abstract: >-
  The Indian PII Robustness Benchmark is a rigorous, multi-lingual evaluation
  framework designed to measure the precision, recall, exact-boundary accuracy,
  and perturbation stability of PII extraction systems in Indian digital contexts.
  Covering 964 canonical evaluation records with 724 gold standard Indian PII
  entities across 5 language regimes and 5 perturbation classes, the benchmark
  evaluates deterministic, off-the-shelf, zero-shot, and Indic-adapted neural systems (B1–B6).
